  "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}x-1, & x<2, \\\\ x-4, & x\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}(-\\frac{3}{2}x-1)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{2}^{5}(x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}-x){|}_{-2}^{2}+(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-4x){|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{3}{4}(2)^{2}-2-(-\\frac{3}{4}(-2)^{2}-(-2))] \\\\  & \\,+[\\frac{{5}^{2}}{2}-4\\cdot 5-(\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-4\\cdot 2))] \\\\  & =[\\,-3-2-(-3+2)]\\,+\\,[\\frac{25}{2}-20-(2-8)] \\\\  & =-4-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
